# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback. Existing static files (assets, /sitemap.xml,
# /robots.txt, /llms.txt, icons) are served first; any other path falls through
# to the app shell so client-side routes (/docs, /compare/*, /alternatives/*,
# /uses/*, /app) resolve on a direct hit or refresh. Status 200 = rewrite, so
# the URL the visitor sees is preserved (important for SEO).

# Retired page — the Astryx theme-generator use case (the Astryx export was
# dropped to keep the export on the core). 301 to the closest live equivalent.
# Specific rule sits ABOVE the catch-all so it wins (first match).
/uses/astryx-theme-generator   /uses/design-system-generator   301

# Retired page — /styles offered a third entrance ("pick a named style") beside
# the two doors, which blurred what the product does: it sold the IDENTITY axis
# as the thing you buy, when the identity is the part that should be yours.
# Same cut as Showcases and Templates.
/styles                        /                               301

# Retired feature — the page templates / `npx uicockpit template` scaffold was cut
# (off-thesis: a design-system generator ships tokens + components + check, not
# ready-made screens). The static /templates/* files are gone, so a plain wildcard
# is safe now; old inbound links land on the live showcase wall.
/templates      /components  301
/templates/*    /components  301
# Showcases retired with the loupe (the app narrowed to one door). The wall of
# real components is the closest surviving evidence, so the links keep landing
# on something rather than 404-ing. Chained redirects are avoided: /templates
# points at /components directly, not via /showcases.
/showcases      /components  301
/showcases/*    /components  301

